# Plugin sync

- `ListReconcile`, `ProgressReconcile`, `LocusReconcile` and `SyncPullKind` are pure and JVM-tested; change decisions
  without `locusSync` stay chapter-URL-only. With `locusSync`, baselines use `PositionBaseline` JSON and same-href
  still enqueues a locus `pos:` op (see seams).
  there and add a test case.
- `TwoWaySync.lock` is one global, non-reentrant `Mutex`. Holders: `run`, `ingestCrawledLists`,
  `pullPositions`, `UpdateChecker.run`, `PluginDataEraser.erase`. Never call one holder from another.
- `tocStored` stays lock-free. `ProgressWriter`'s `onWritten` hook must not call `drain`.
- `sync.json` changes go through `SyncStateStore.update` (locked read-modify-write); list files
  `_lists/*.txt` have no lock of their own.
- Baselines record what both sides last agreed on. Check the order of baseline writes against
  `docs/agent/seams.md` before moving any of them.
- Position writes go through `data/ProgressWriter.kt`; logging through `debug/DebugLog.kt`.
- Plugin-visible changes follow `docs/agent/cross-repo.md` and `.cursor/rules/plugin-api.mdc`.

Before changing a file here, run `rg -n '<FileName>' docs/agent/seams.md`.

